				application: "E.O. 111 does exactly what the invalidated part of E.O. 464 did: it makes the named officials' appearance before Congress depend on the President's prior approval, without requiring the President to state, case by case, which specific piece of information is privileged and why. This effectively gives the Executive a blanket veto over Sec. 21 inquiries into its own affairs.",
