			factPattern: "<span class='bar-tag'>2026 BAR EXAM — Q.5</span> The House Committee on Good Government investigates how a provincial government used its share of excise taxes on cigarettes. Some provincial officials give evasive answers, so the Committee cites them in contempt and has them detained. The officials file a petition for habeas corpus with the Court of Appeals. After hearings, the CA issues the writ and orders the officials' provisional release. Displeased with the CA's ruling, the House issues a show-cause order against the three CA Justices who signed it, directing them to explain why they should not be cited in contempt by the House.",
